From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 07:52:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 20/21] serial: samsung_tty: release an optional reset in probe

Some SoCs (Nexell S5P6818) leave secondary UARTs held in reset by the
bootloader - the controller reads back 0 and never works. Get an optional
reset in probe and deassert it before touching the port. Harmless where
no reset is wired (NULL), e.g. the console UART the bootloader set up.

Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
---
 drivers/tty/serial/samsung_tty.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/tty/serial/samsung_tty.c b/drivers/tty/serial/samsung_tty.c
index 2674d9517..ab34bf24c 100644
--- a/drivers/tty/serial/samsung_tty.c
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/samsung_tty.c
@@ -34,6 +34,7 @@
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
+#include <linux/reset.h>
 #include <linux/serial.h>
 #include <linux/serial_core.h>
 #include <linux/serial_s3c.h>
@@ -1955,6 +1956,20 @@ static int s3c24xx_serial_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	}
 	ourport = &s3c24xx_serial_ports[index];
 
+	/*
+	 * Some SoCs (e.g. Nexell S5P6818) leave secondary UARTs held in reset
+	 * by the bootloader. Release an optional reset before touching the
+	 * controller; harmless (NULL) where no reset is wired (e.g. the console).
+	 */
+	if (np) {
+		struct reset_control *rst =
+			devm_reset_control_get_optional_exclusive(&pdev->dev, NULL);
+
+		if (IS_ERR(rst))
+			return PTR_ERR(rst);
+		reset_control_deassert(rst);
+	}
+
 	s3c24xx_serial_init_port_default(index);
 
 	ourport->drv_data = s3c24xx_get_driver_data(pdev);
